---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

const updated = 'October 23, 2026';

const toc = [
  { id: 'acceptance', label: 'Acceptance' },
  { id: 'the-service', label: 'The service' },
  { id: 'your-content', label: 'Your content' },
  { id: 'acceptable-use', label: 'Acceptable use' },
  { id: 'no-professional-advice', label: 'No professional advice' },
  { id: 'intellectual-property', label: 'Intellectual property' },
  { id: 'advertising', label: 'Advertising' },
  { id: 'third-parties', label: 'Third-party services' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
  { id: 'disclaimer', label: 'Disclaimer' },
  { id: 'liability', label: 'Limitation of liability' },
  { id: 'indemnity', label: 'Indemnity' },
  { id: 'governing-law', label: 'Governing law' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];

const highlights = [
  { value: 'Free', label: 'No account or payment required' },
  { value: 'Yours', label: 'You keep the rights to your images' },
  { value: 'Best-effort', label: 'Verify the export before sharing' },
];

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Terms & Conditions',
  url: 'https://imageredaction.com/terms',
  description:
    'The rules for using Redact: free to use, your images stay yours, advertising is consent-controlled, and the tool is best-effort.',
  dateModified: '2026-10-23',
  publisher: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Redact',
    url: 'https://imageredaction.com/',
    email: 'hello@imageredaction.com',
  },
};
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions"
  description="The rules for using Redact, in plain language: it is free to use, your images stay yours, and you are responsible for checking the result before you share it."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  updated={updated}
  toc={toc}
  highlights={highlights}
  summary="Redact is a free, browser-based tool. You keep the rights to your images, you are responsible for how you use the output, and the redaction is best-effort — always check the exported file before you send it."
  schema={schema}
>
  <section id="acceptance">
    <h2>Acceptance of these terms</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms & Conditions (“terms”) govern your use of imageredaction.com and the
      Redact editor (together, “the service”). By accessing or using the service, you
      agree to these terms and to the{' '}
      <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, please do not
      use the service.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you use the service on behalf of an organisation, you confirm that you have
      authority to bind that organisation to these terms. You must be old enough to
      consent to using an online service where you live.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="the-service">
    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>
      Redact is a free, browser-based tool for covering parts of images. It runs on your
      device, requires an internet connection and no account, and does not upload your
      files. The current version is provided free of charge. If paid features are
      introduced, their prices and terms will be shown before any purchase.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may add, change, suspend, or discontinue any part of the service at any time.
      We do not guarantee that the service will always be available, error-free, or
      compatible with every browser or file.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="your-content">
    <h2>Your content</h2>
    <p>
      You keep all rights to the images you use with Redact. Because the files are
      processed locally, we do not receive, store, own, or license your images. We claim
      no ownership over your content or your exports.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are responsible for the content you process and share. You must have the
      right to use and edit the image, and you must have permission to handle any
      personal information it contains. Do not use the service to process content you
      are not allowed to process.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are also responsible for the final result. A redaction box only covers what it
      covers, and an automated check is not a guarantee. Review the exported image
      before you send it anywhere.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="acceptable-use">
    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree not to use the service to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>break any applicable law or regulation;</li>
      <li>infringe someone else’s copyright, privacy, or other rights;</li>
      <li>
        harass, threaten, defraud, or deceive anyone, or to conceal evidence or evade a
        lawful process;
      </li>
      <li>
        interfere with the security, availability, or operation of the site, including
        by attempting to gain unauthorised access or by automating requests in a way
        that burdens the service;
      </li>
      <li>
        misrepresent a redacted image as certified, compliant, or safe when it has not
        been properly checked;
      </li>
      <li>distribute malware or use the site as part of an unlawful scheme.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may restrict or block access if we reasonably believe these rules have been
      broken, or if a request threatens the service or another person.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="no-professional-advice">
    <h2>No professional advice</h2>
    <p>
      Redact is a utility, not legal, compliance, privacy, or security advice. A
      redaction produced with the tool may not satisfy a regulator, court, employer,
      platform, or counterparty. Nothing on this site creates a professional
      relationship.
    </p>
    <p>
      Smart detection, OCR, and verification are best-effort. They can miss text,
      faces, codes, and other details, and blur or pixelation can sometimes be partially
      reconstructed. Use ink black for identity and financial details, and get
      professional advice when the stakes require it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="intellectual-property">
    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The site’s design, copy, and original code are owned by us or used with
      permission. You may not copy, modify, or redistribute the site’s branding or
      content except as allowed by law or with written permission.
    </p>
    <p>
      Third-party components remain under their own licences. For example, Tesseract.js
      and MediaPipe are used under their open-source licences, and the Inter typeface is
      used under the SIL Open Font License. Using the tool does not give you ownership
      of any part of the service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="advertising">
    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      The service is free. Advertising may be enabled to support it. When advertising
      is enabled, ads are served by Google AdSense under the consent banner described
      in the <a href="/privacy-policy#advertising">Privacy Policy</a>. Advertising is
      optional: rejecting non-essential storage does not block the editor.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ads are provided by third parties. We do not control which ads appear, and an ad
      does not mean we endorse the product or service it promotes. Any transaction you
      enter into with an advertiser is between you and that advertiser.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="third-parties">
    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Smart detection loads the Tesseract.js library and language data from jsDelivr,
      and Detect faces loads the MediaPipe vision library from jsDelivr plus a small
      face model from Google Cloud Storage. When advertising is enabled, the page also
      loads Google AdSense from Google’s advertising domains. Those services have their
      own terms and privacy practices, and their availability is outside our control.
      We are not responsible for third-party services or for the content of external
      sites we link to.
    </p>
    <p>
      Manual redaction, copy, and export do not depend on the detection, PDF, or
      advertising requests.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms from time to time. The date near the top of this page
      shows the latest version. Changes take effect when they are posted. Continuing to
      use the service after an update means you accept the revised terms. If you do not
      agree, stop using the service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="disclaimer">
    <h2>Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, the service is provided “as is” and “as
      available”, without warranties of any kind, express or implied. That includes
      implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose,
      non-infringement, accuracy, and uninterrupted or error-free operation.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not warrant that detection will find every sensitive detail, that a
      redaction cannot be reversed, or that the output will meet the requirements of any
      organisation or law. You are responsible for verifying the result.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="liability">
    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, we will not be liable for indirect,
      incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for loss of data,
      profits, goodwill, or business opportunity, arising from your use of, or inability
      to use, the service.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our total liability for any claim relating to the service will not exceed the
      greater of the amount you paid us in the twelve months before the claim, or fifty
      US dollars (USD 50). Some jurisdictions do not allow certain limitations, so parts
      of this section may not apply to you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="indemnity">
    <h2>Indemnity</h2>
    <p>
      You agree to indemnify and hold harmless Redact and its operator from claims,
      damages, losses, and expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising from your
      use of the service, the content you process, or your breach of these terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="governing-law">
    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of India, without regard to conflict-of-law
      principles. Subject to any consumer protection rights that cannot be waived,
      disputes will be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts in
      India.
    </p>
    <p>
      If any part of these terms is found unenforceable, the remaining parts stay in
      effect. These terms and the Privacy Policy are the entire agreement between you
      and us about the service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms:{' '}
      <a href="mailto:hello@imageredaction.com">hello@imageredaction.com</a>, or use the{' '}
      <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. For information about how the site handles
      data, read the <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
